                    <!--!-->2500<!--!-->
                    Nov 22nd</span> - <!--!--><!--!--><a href="http://the-hoops.co.uk" target="_blank" title="Click for pubs website">Hoops</a><!--!-->
    , Barton<!--!-->,
        <!--!--><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&amp;destination=52.182344,0.056850" target="_blank" title="Click for venue map">CB23 7BD</a>  - Tel: 01223 344 995<!--!-->
                <br>Hare: <!--!--><span>Jetstream and Unmentionable</span><!--!--><br><span notes=""><!--!-->Back to the venue of the very first Cambridge Hash Run. New Landlord, Steve previously from the Elm Tree and Cambridge Rugby Club, is looking forward to our visit. He has agreed that we can all bring plates of sandwiches, snacks and cake for a buffet to share in the pub. Slightly different trail so hopefully nobody will get shot, either on the rifle range or by the not so friendly farmer! </span></div><div class="nextRun"><span link=""><!--!-->
                    Run
                    <!--!-->2498<!--!-->
                    Nov 8th</span> - <!--!--><!--!--><a href="http://www.therfieldfoxandduck.co.uk" target="_blank" title="Click for pubs website">Fox and Duck</a><!--!-->
    , Therfield<!--!-->,
        <!--!--><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&amp;destination=52.017349,-0.054246" target="_blank" title="Click for venue map">SG8 9PN</a>  - Tel: 01763 287 246<!--!-->
                <br>Hare: <!--!--><span>Kermit and Hooker</span><!--!--><br><span notes=""><!--!-->This is the 1st r*n here for 14 years. Please phone if you want to eat.</span></div><h3>October 2026</h3><div><span link=""><!--!-->
                    Run
                    <!--!-->2496<!--!-->
                    Oct 25th</span> - <!--!--><!--!--><a href="https://www.facebook.com/thechequerswrestlingworth" target="_blank" title="Click for pubs website">Chequers</a><!--!-->
    , Wrestlingworth<!--!-->,
        <!--!--><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&amp;destination=52.111048,-0.164958" target="_blank" title="Click for venue map">SG19 2EP</a>  - Tel: 01767 631 818<!--!-->
                <br>Hare: <!--!--><span>Haven't Got One, Seamus and Paddy </span><!--!--><br><span notes=""><!--!-->DO NOT GO TO PUB FIRST! The trail starts and ends at Hatley Village Hall, 1 Main Street, Hatley St George, Cambridgeshire, <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&amp;destination=52.141028,-0.126032" target="_blank" title="Click for map">SG19 3HW</a>. We will have use of the car park and toilets only. No muddy shoes in the hall please and leave no mess, as yours truly will need to clean it up!</span></div></div></div></body></html>
